From f671e4e6bf9fc805fb765a29e407fb2520d4515f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ond=C5=99ej=20=C5=A0imon?= <ondrej@dorhawk.software>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:24:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Refuse a bitmap whose bits don't fit 32 bits.

FileZilla quit when a site was deleted in its Site Manager. wxWidgets
asks SHGetStockIconInfo for the question icon with SHGSI_SYSICONINDEX;
Wine's stub answers shell32.dll with icon -1, and wx then extracts it
at size -1, which reaches CreateIconFromResourceEx as 65535 x 65535.

NtGdiCreateBitmap computed the size of the bits as INT * INT. At
65535 x 65535 x 32 bpp that overflows, which C leaves undefined, and
clang dropped the dib_stride != size / height check that followed. The
bitmap was made (16 GiB), drawing the icon into it faulted inside
NtUserGetIconInfo with the USER lock held, and the next CreateWindow
(the confirmation dialog) asserted on the held lock.

The size is now computed in SIZE_T, and bits that don't fit 32 bits
fail with ERROR_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY, as Windows XP does (gdi32's
test_bitmap accepts it).

Tested with a program that creates a 65535 x 65535 bitmap, extracts
shell32's icon at size -1 and then creates a window: before, the bitmap
was made and the window's creation hit "BUG: holding USER lock" (exit
1); after, the bitmap is refused with error 8, the icon is NULL and the
window is made (exit 0). FileZilla 3.72.1 then showed its "Do you
really want to delete the selected entries?" question instead of
quitting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/win32u/bitmap.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/bitmap.c b/dlls/win32u/bitmap.c
index 97b5cf9f7c..f872576508 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/bitmap.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/bitmap.c
@@ -275,11 +275,14 @@ HBITMAP WINAPI NtGdiCreateBitmap( INT width, INT height, UINT planes,
     }
 
     dib_stride = get_dib_stride( width, bpp );
-    size = dib_stride * height;
-    /* Check for overflow (dib_stride itself must be ok because of the constraint on bm.bmWidth above). */
-    if (dib_stride != size / height)
+    /* In 64 bits: as two INTs the product overflowed, which C leaves undefined, and the check
+     * that followed was compiled away, so a 65535 x 65535 icon (16 GiB at 32 bpp) was created
+     * and drawing into it faulted with the USER lock held. Bits that don't fit 32 bits fail
+     * as not enough memory, as XP does (see test_bitmap in gdi32's tests). */
+    size = (SIZE_T)dib_stride * height;
+    if (size > 0xffffffff)
     {
-        RtlSetLastWin32Error( ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER );
+        RtlSetLastWin32Error( ERROR_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY );
         return 0;
     }
 
